From c43be997786443a74fbcdeba4e8bba37c2fcf8ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alain Volmat <alain.volmat@foss.st.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 15:45:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] spi: stm32: abort probe on gen_pool alloc failure

Probe should be aborted properly when gen_pool allocation
(gen_pool_dma_zalloc) failed during the driver probe is
a DMA-MDMA chaining has been indicated within the device-tree.

Fixes: d17dd2f1d8a1 ("spi: stm32: use STM32 DMA with STM32 MDMA to enhance DDR use")

Signed-off-by: Alain Volmat <alain.volmat@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I0d6326b02c5e6ee4c9094578c9d12f88cc9a0c58
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/583805
Reviewed-by: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Alain VOLMAT <alain.volmat@st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Tested-by: Alain VOLMAT <alain.volmat@st.com>
---
 drivers/spi/spi-stm32.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/spi/spi-stm32.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-stm32.c
@@ -2523,7 +2523,9 @@ static int stm32_spi_probe(struct platfo
 		spi->sram_rx_buf = gen_pool_dma_zalloc(spi->sram_pool, spi->sram_rx_buf_size,
 						       &spi->sram_dma_rx_buf);
 		if (!spi->sram_rx_buf) {
+			ret = -ENOMEM;
 			dev_err(&pdev->dev, "failed to allocate SRAM buffer\n");
+			goto err_pool_free;
 		} else {
 			spi->mdma_rx = dma_request_chan(spi->dev, "rxm2m");
 			if (IS_ERR(spi->mdma_rx)) {
